hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24266","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, from his father: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Would you like a foster daughter of ours for you to care for? He said: I think it was Zaynab. Then he came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him about her and said: What has the girl done? He said: I left her with her mother. He said: Then what brings you, what have you come for? He said: I have come for you to teach me something to say at my sleep. So he said: Recite: Say, O you disbelievers, then sleep upon its seal, for it is a disavowal of polytheism."
"24267","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, from his father, and he was a foster father to Umm Salamah, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What brings you, what have you come for? He said: I have come for you to teach me something to say at my sleep. He said: Recite Say, O you disbelievers, at your sleep, for it is a disavowal of polytheism."
"24268","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Farwah ibn Nawfal al-Ashja'i, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to a man: Recite at your sleep, for it is a disavowal of polytheism: Say, O you disbelievers."
"24269","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Farwah al-Ashja'i, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to a man: Recite at your sleep: Say, O you disbelievers, for it is a disavowal of polytheism."
